{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1504186915,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEyMjk1Njg1NTY="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1504187504,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNjMwMTY3NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1776#issuecomment-326301674"},"message":"Yes, we could refactor but we will need to check the code first if we ever rely on passing entire or sanitized environment. I remember in at least one case (probably more) just updating os.environ. one use case, when sanitization is needed for some env variables, setting their value to none in the dictionary could signal that they needed to be removed (still allowing for an empty string)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1504187527,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNjMwMTc5MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1776#issuecomment-326301790"},"message":"I wouldn't call it a bug though ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1504187647,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNjMwMjQwMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1776#issuecomment-326302402"},"message":"Well, I'm not sure. I tend to agree we should update instead. But: That would mean we have no way to have full control of the environment a call is running in. Might be troublesome.\nHowever, there is a way in between. `Runner` also has an attribute `env`, which can be set via `__init__()`. May be the default for this attribute should be `os.environ` and the `env` parameter of `run()` should update this one. As of now the default is just empty.\nThat way we can easily set up a `Runner` instance with full customized environment if needed.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1504187745,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNjMwMjkwNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1776#issuecomment-326302904"},"message":"Additional note: In any case this also requires to adapt `GitRunner`. Just saying, so we are aware.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1504189084,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNjMwOTU1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1776#issuecomment-326309559"},"message":"OK, I can feel the anxiety...\n\nNo full control: I am making an explicit call to `run()`, I pass the env var -- I am in control.\n\nBut what happens is that ANY command will fail, because it expects a tailored environment that I have no idea about. Hence, when I set `env=` things break.\n\nWe can call this a feature, but we have no such tag.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1504189408,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNjMxMTMyNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1776#issuecomment-326311327"},"message":"It seems that this is the only code that needs changing for my particular issue:\n\n```py\n    @staticmethod\n    def get_git_environ_adjusted(env=None):\n        \"\"\"\n        Replaces GIT_DIR and GIT_WORK_TREE with absolute paths if relative path and defined\n        \"\"\"\n        # if env set copy else get os environment\n        git_env = env.copy() if env else os.environ.copy()\n ````\n\nenv should update os.environ and not replace it.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1504190998,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNjMxOTc0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1776#issuecomment-326319748"},"message":"Re \"the only code to be changed\":\nWould work, but leads to an inconsistency, I think. Once at it, we should do it similarly if `Runner` is used directly instead of using `GitRunner`.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1507443813,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzNDk4NjIyOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1776#issuecomment-334986228"},"message":"There is no interest in this...","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1507443813,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTI4MzA4ODk5NQ=="},"status":2}]}